# Keep the Docker build context small + reproducible. The AOT build only needs sources.
**/bin/
**/obj/
.git/
.github/
.vs/
.idea/
**/*.user
# Every one of these is build or agent output, and each pattern is anchored the way Docker actually reads it:
# a leading-slash-free pattern like `TestResults/` still matches only at the context ROOT, so `Tests/TestResults`
# was shipped in full — 994 MB of it on 2026-08-15, inside a 1.17 GB context (XC-62).
**/coverage/
**/TestResults/
**/BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/
artifacts/
# .claude/ is agent memory, transcripts and scratch — 98.8 MB measured, 74% of the whole context, and it is
# rewritten constantly. The build stage is `COPY . .`, so it also invalidated that layer's cache on every run
# even when no source had changed. Nothing in the image comes from it.
.claude/
# Exclude docs from the image context EXCEPT openapi.yaml, which Server.csproj embeds at compile time
# (GET /openapi.yaml + Swagger UI serve it from the self-contained binary). Without the negation the AOT
# publish fails: CS1566 "Could not find /src/docs/openapi.yaml".
docs/*
!docs/openapi.yaml
Demo/
UI/
# Never ship models / fixtures into the image — they are large and provided at runtime.
*.gguf
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.7z
**/test_fixtures/
*.wav
*.mp3
